## Why This Is Asked
Tests for autosave/drafts cover offline-first UX, idempotent writes, and cross-device conflicts, which are common pain points in real apps.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first data flows and write queuing
- Idempotent REST writes and ordering guarantees
- Test data isolation via seeds and reset hooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright skeleton (pseudo)
test('autosave offline queue and merge', async ({ page, request }) => {
  await page.goto('/editor');
  await page.fill('#note', 'Initial');
  await page.waitForTimeout(31000); // wait for autosave
  // simulate offline
  await page.route('POST', '/api/drafts', route => route.abort());
  await page.fill('#note', 'Offline edit');
  await page.setOfflineMode(true);
  await page.fill('#note', 'More offline edits');
  await page.setOfflineMode(false);
  // verify upload order and no duplicates
  // reload or inspect draft store
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt this for WebSocket-based drafting?
- How would you test long offline periods and partial merges?

## Why This Is Asked
Offline-first reliability with service workers is a critical requirement in modern e-commerce applications. This question evaluates whether a candidate understands how to test caching behavior, connectivity state changes, and retry logic in end-to-end tests.

## Key Concepts
- Offline-first UX patterns with service workers
- Network throttling and failure simulation (Cypress or Playwright network interception)
- Test data isolation with fixtures or unique identifiers
- Idempotent order placement to prevent duplicate charges

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: Intercept network requests to simulate offline behavior
cy.intercept('POST', '/api/payment', (req) => {
  req.reply({ statusCode: 503, body: { error: 'Network error' } });
}).as('paymentRequest');

// Simulate going offline
cy.networkIdle(); // or use Cypress offline plugin
cy.window().then((win) => {
  win.navigator.onLine = false;
});

// Verify offline UI and localStorage persistence
cy.get('[data-testid=offline-banner]').should('be.visible');
cy.getLocalStorage('cart').should('exist');

// Restore network and retry
cy.networkOn();
cy.wait('@paymentRequest').then(() => {
  cy.get('[data-testid=order-confirmation]').should('be.visible');
});

// Verify idempotent order creation
cy.get('@paymentRequest').its('response.statusCode').should('eq', 200);
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design end-to-end tests for multi-region, multi-tenant feature flags, covering UI, API, and background workers, with rapid toggling and race conditions. Demonstrates seeds, isolation strategies, and SLA verification.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flag precedence and propagation across layers
- Cross-region consistency (UI, API, workers)
- Concurrency, load testing, and idempotency

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold for E2E feature-flag toggles
async function testFlagToggle(tenantId, flagKey, value) {
  await api.setFlag(tenantId, flagKey, value);
  await wait(50);
  const uiState = await ui.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  const workerState = await worker.getFlagState(tenantId, flagKey);
  if (uiState !== value || workerState !== value) throw new Error('Inconsistent state');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure cross-region propagation latency? 
- How do you handle partial failures (region down) and ensure eventual consistency?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests that exercise keyboard accessibility demonstrate familiarity with a11y concepts and deterministic testing approaches for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Keyboard navigation and focus management
- ARIA roles and attributes (role=dialog, aria-label, aria-live)
- Test determinism with seeded localStorage and deterministic delays

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test outline in Cypress
describe('Keyboard accessibility for notes', () => {
  it('navigates via Tab, opens modal, saves, edits, deletes, and persists', () => {
    // seed
    window.localStorage.setItem('notes', JSON.stringify([
      { id: 1, title: 'Note 1', body: 'Body 1' },
      { id: 2, title: 'Note 2', body: 'Body 2' }
    ]));

    cy.visit('/');

    // Tab through list and verify focus
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.focused().should('have.attr', 'role', 'listitem');

    // Open create modal with keyboard
    cy.get('[data-testid="create-button"]').focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[role="dialog"]').should('be.visible');

    // Create note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').type('New Note');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-body"]').type('New Body');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Edit existing note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').clear().type('Edited Title');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Delete note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.get('[data-testid="delete-button"]').click();

    // Verify persistence after reload
    cy.reload();
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const notes = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('notes'));
      expect(notes).to.have.length(2);
    });
  });
});
```

